      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T10:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay so in the end, pvmfw receives a single DTBO instead of a set of DTBOs (one per \"assignable unit\") so how will pvmfw be able to detect that incompatible/partial subsets of those assignable units have been assigned?\n\nFor example, if two devices are in the same IOMMU group, doesn\u0027t pvmfw need to validate that they actually share a pvIOMMU group? Or did we conclude that this part of validation had been moved to the hypervisor so that pvmfw\u0027s validation work is reduced to a per-device granularity, @smostafa@google.com?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "04c3ea414f47f77dc50e521d35d68b85eaea0e83",
