        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T10:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This error is raised when the header version doesn\u0027t support the entry index (which type-checking forces to always be _valid_, for at least one version) so I\u0027m worried that this error message might be misleading. Could we rework it to also contain the version (which, on a side note, it might be wise to turn into its own type, I recon?) e.g.\n```\nSelf::Unsupported((major, minor)) \u003d\u003e write!(f, \"Not supported by version {major}.{minor}\")\n```\nResulting in the combined error message:\n```\nInvalid Entry::VmDtbo entry: Not supported by version 1.0\n```\ninstead of what would currently be generated:\n```\nInvalid Entry::VmDtbo entry: Invalid entry index: 2\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 95,
        "startChar": 52,
        "endLine": 95,
        "endChar": 80
      },
      "revId": "04c3ea414f47f77dc50e521d35d68b85eaea0e83",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6888da5_200e9c7c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/config.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 135,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-02T10:36:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you introduce a private method to get the `entries` as a slice, abstracting away the management of a maximum index, e.g.\n```\nfn entries(\u0026self) -\u003e Result\u003c\u0026[HeaderEntry]\u003e {\n    let last_entry \u003d match self.version {\n        Header::VERSION_1_0 \u003d\u003e Entry::DebugPolicy,\n        Header::VERSION_1_1 \u003d\u003e Entry::VmDtbo,\n        _ \u003d\u003e {\n            let (major, minor) \u003d self.version_tuple();\n            return Err(Error::UnsupportedVersion(major, minor));\n        }\n    };\n\n    Ok(\u0026self.entries[..\u003d(last_entry as usize)])\n}\n```\nwhich should then allow you to bound-check in the usual way\n```\nlet (offset, size) \u003d if let Some(e) \u003d self.entries().get(entry_index) {\n    (e.offset as usize, e.size as usize)\n} else {\n    return Err(Error::InvalidEntry(entry, ...));\n};\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 128,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 135,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "04c3ea414f47f77dc50e521d35d68b85eaea0e83",
